ty on coal and carbon. During WWII, she researched the physical structure of coal to understand how it could be used for better gas masks. She discovered how the pores in carbon change at a molecular level when heated, leading to her identifying the difference between \"graphitizing\" and \"non-graphitizing\" carbons. This work remains fundamental to carbon-fiber technology and space shuttle heat shields today.\nTo get the single image for which the credit was due, X had to expose a tiny fiber of ___ to a narrow beam of X-rays for 62 to 100 hours while maintaining 92% humidity in a hydrogen-filled chamber. She wasn't just taking a picture; she was performing a mathematical feat. She used Bragg's Law to calculate the distances between atoms based on the diffraction spots. She had actually calculated the structure in her lab notes before the credit was stolen. Id X and Y. ‎", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:48:49Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "franklin", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:48:50Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "rosalind", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:48:51Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "dna", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:48:58Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "x-ray crystallography", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:48:59Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "Question me hai waise toh", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:49:02Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Question me reh gaya", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-16T15:49:02Z",